---
.title = "Dynamic Array (ArrayList)",
.date = "2026-10-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

`std.ArrayList` is the standard library's growable contiguous array buffer.

In Zig 0.16, `std.ArrayList(T)` is unmanaged by default and initialized with `.empty`. Operations requiring memory allocation or release explicitly accept an `Allocator` parameter:

- `append(allocator, item)`: Append a single element to the end;
- `appendSlice(allocator, items)`: Append a slice of elements;
- `insert(allocator, index, item)`: Insert an element at the specified index (O(N));
- `orderedRemove(index)`: Remove the element at index while preserving order (O(N));
- `swapRemove(index)`: Fast removal by swapping with the last element (O(1), order not preserved);
- `pop()`: Pop and return the last element;
- `deinit(allocator)`: Release allocated storage.

